: Houten</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moser</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalton</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><source>Survey methods in social investigation</source><year>1971</year><edition>2</edition><publisher-name>Aldershot: Gower</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McColl</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use and design of questionnaires</article-title><source>Royal College of General Practitioners: London</source><year>2000</year></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sinclair</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Berwiczonek</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Thurston</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bulloch</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellery</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Giesbrecht</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of an evidence-based education program for pressure ulcer prevention</article-title><source>Journal of Wound, Ostomy and Continence Nursing</source><year>2004</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>50</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gunningberg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pressure ulcer prevention: evaluation of an education programme for Swedish nurses</article-title><source>Journal of Wound care</source><year>2004</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>89</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15045800</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B33"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Streiner</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Norman</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name></person-group><source>Health Measurement Scales: A Practical Guide to their Development and Use</source><year>2003</year><edition>3</edition><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B34"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duimel</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Massage to prevent pressure ulcers: knowledge, beliefs, practice and effectiveness [Thesis]</article-title><source>Drukkerij Duplica</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Maastricht: Maastricht University</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jolley</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>McGowan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hickey</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Campbell</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinclair</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Montgomery</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Preventing pressure ulcers with the Australian Medical Sheepskin: an open-label randomised controlled trial</article-title><source>The Medical journal of Australia</source><year>2004</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>324</fpage><lpage>327</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15059051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xakell